sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-24--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-anthrobots-24: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.23";
    dc:description "Human and frog genomes are obviously divergent, and both labs produced motile epithelial spheroids. That pair of facts does not separate a generic morphogenetic law from ordinary shared mechanics of ciliated epithelia. Nothing now public, and no reanalysis of genomes or shapes, would count as a confirmation or a refutation of the extra inference.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Genomic distance between human and Xenopus, and similarity of the two motile spheroids, can both be measured. No outcome distinguishes 'generic laws of morphogenesis matter in addition to the genome' from both epithelia obeying the same packing and cilia mechanics in similar culture conditions.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Morphological similarity of two ciliated spheroids is expected from shared culture physics without a further law.", "The statement does not name a law, a prediction or a rival model that existing genomes or shapes could reject.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.68"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.227"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-24--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2024-anthrobots-24 by Grok 4.7: 0.3";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
